# =================================================== #
                PROBLEM DESCRITION
# =================================================== #

Table: Products

+---------------+---------+
| Column Name   | Type    |
+---------------+---------+
| product_id    | int     |
| new_price     | int     |
| change_date   | date    |
+---------------+---------+

(product_id, change_date) is the primary key (combination of columns with unique values) of this table.

Each row of this table indicates that the price of some product was changed to a new price at some date.

Initially, all products have price 10.

Write a solution to find the prices of all products on the date 2019-08-16.

Return the result table in any order.

# =================================================== #
                      SOLUTION
# =================================================== #

import pandas as pd

def price_at_given_date(products: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:

    idx_dates = (
        products
        .loc[products['change_date'] <= '2019-08-16']
        .groupby(by = 'product_id')['change_date']
        .idxmax()
    )
    
    prices = (
        products
        .loc[idx_dates, ['product_id', 'new_price']]
        .set_index('product_id')
    )

    result = pd.DataFrame({'product_id' : products['product_id'].unique()})
    result['price'] = result['product_id'].map(prices['new_price']).fillna(value = 10)

    return result
